## 1. Site structure — the sections the dashboard should have

The live site currently shows three top-level ideas in its copy: **"The week"** (a status board — "Needs someone assigned," "Needs a closer look"), **"Next visit assignment"** (pick a visit → ranked recommendation), and **"How the work is spread"** (a workload view). Formalize these into four persistent sections plus one new one, all reachable from a single nav bar so the tool stays a one-page operational surface, not a multi-app suite:

| Section | Current state on live site | What to build/refine |
|---|---|---|
| **1. The Week** | Shows a status board, "Needs someone assigned" / "Needs a closer look" | Keep as the landing view. Add a visible **"last synced: X minutes ago"** badge (per §4) and a red/amber/green state per visit row reflecting evidence sufficiency (§3), not just assignment status. |
| **2. Next Visit Assignment** | "Pick a visit. The board checks every calendar, rules out who cannot go, and explains who it would send." | This is the ranking screen — refine per §2/§3 hard-gate and scoring logic. Every recommendation must show its **reason string**, not just a name and score. |
| **3. How the Work Is Spread** | Workload view, described as "Record" | Keep as the equity/audit view — out-of-hours tally, visit count per coordinator, van-trained utilization. This is where §7's equity metrics surface. |
| **4. Sync Calendars (new)** | Not yet present as a distinct section | New dedicated screen: upload panel + review overlay per §4. This should NOT be buried inside "Next Visit Assignment" — it is its own workflow step because it produces the evidence that step 2 consumes. |
| **5. Data & Exports (new)** | Not yet present | New section for CSV import/export and audit-trail download, per §5. |

Each section keeps the same visual language already on the site ("Record" labels, card-based layout) — this prompt is about wiring real logic and data behind the existing frontend shell, not restyling it.

