## 5. Uploads and exports — the two data-movement flows the dashboard needs

This is new relative to the earlier prompts and directly answers "uploads, export stuff maintained properly":

### 5.1 Uploads
- **Calendar images** (§4) — per-coordinator, day/work-week view only, one file per upload slot.
- **Participant/visit roster import** — a CSV upload matching the Access export columns already in use (Visit Month, Ideal Date, Status, Child/Parent names, Address + drive time, Childcare flag, Van Inaccessible flag, Scheduling Notes, Contact Notes) so the lab can migrate data out of Access incrementally rather than needing a big-bang cutover. Validate on upload: reject rows with an unparseable Ideal Date, flag (don't reject) rows missing drive-time data since that only affects the offer-window calculation, not core scheduling validity.
- **Reliability matrix updates** — a small structured upload (or an admin-only in-app edit form) for updating a coordinator's `RELIABLE`/`IN_TRAINING` status per assessment, so the matrix doesn't require a code change every time someone completes training. This directly answers the meeting's own note: "as people continue training, I will add in who's [reliable] on this."

### 5.2 Exports
- **Ranked-assignment audit export (CSV)** — every assignment decision made through the dashboard, with participant ID, visit month, chosen coordinator(s), score, reason string, evidence tier/timestamp used, and whether it was a hard-override case (NDD, 36m manual, 24m remote). This is the record that lets Dr. Bradshaw or a new scheduler reconstruct *why* a past assignment happened.
- **Workload/equity export (CSV)** — a snapshot of the "How the Work Is Spread" section: visits per coordinator, out-of-hours tally, van-trained utilization — for the periodic fairness review the manual already does manually via the Slack canvas.
- **Calendar-sync evidence export** — per sync run, which blocks were detected, which were confirmed vs. corrected by a human, and the resulting `vision_correction_rate` — this is the metric that eventually justifies turning on auto-commit for a given coordinator.

All exports should be triggerable from the "Data & Exports" section (§1, section 5) as a simple "Download CSV" action — no scheduled/emailed exports needed for this build; on-demand is sufficient and matches the same "sync when you need it, not constantly" philosophy the lab already applied to calendar syncing.

