## 6. Additional considerations carried over and finalized

- **Communication method field.** Surface `preferred_contact_method` (Text/Email/Call) directly next to every visit in "Next Visit Assignment" — this was an explicit open item from the meeting ("confirm current family communication method") and belongs beside the ranked coordinators, not in a separate settings page.
- **Scheduling notes stay free-text.** Family-specific quirks (fragrance sensitivity, weekend-only availability) are too heterogeneous to rule-encode — keep this a visible free-text field surfaced prominently next to the ranked list, never parsed or auto-applied as a constraint.
- **PTO / explicit unavailability.** No special-case logic — a coordinator's marked-out dates simply appear as `Busy` blocks through the same sync pipeline as any other calendar evidence.
- **NDD visit duration.** Automatically add 60 minutes to the base visit-length lookup when `is_ndd_cross_collab` is true, and make sure this adjusted duration — not the static manual table — feeds the calendar-conflict window check, or NDD visits will be under-blocked and risk double-booking.
- **Travel-time-adjusted offer windows.** The earliest/latest offerable start time for a given visit is a function of that specific family's drive time, not a fixed lab-hours assumption — compute it per visit from the stored address/drive-time field, and use the same computed window in both the scheduler's ranking view and any future family-facing display, so the two can never disagree.
- **Scope boundary, confirmed again:** this dashboard is scheduler-facing only. No family-facing self-scheduling calendar is part of this build — that was explicitly set aside in the meeting ("let's just keep the family thing aside... this is for us").

